      "page_content": "1. Purpose\nThis policy defines the methodology used to measure the value of Order Intake for multi-element arrangements,\nincluding allocation of contract value across deliverables using Standalone Selling Price (SSP).\n2. Scope\nApplies to all multi-element customer arrangements combining:\n- Hardware/Software (HW/SW) deliverables, AND\n- Services deliverables\n3. Definitions\nStandalone Selling Price (SSP): The price at which the Company would sell a deliverable separately under similar\ncircumstances.\n4. Roles and Responsibilities\nRole | Responsibility\nDeal Desk | Prepares SSP allocation calculations\nFinance Manager | Reviews allocations exceeding variance threshold\nPricing Team | Maintains standard list price catalogue\n5. SSP Allocation Methodology\n5.1 Calculation Basis\nAllocation is performed using the Standalone List Price method. Each deliverable is allocated a share of total contract\nvalue based on its list price relative to total list price of all deliverables. No weighting adjustment is applied.\n5.2 Allocation Formula\nSSP Allocation (Deliverable) = (List Price of Deliverable ÷ Total List Price of All Deliverables) × Total Contract Value\n6. Sample Allocation Illustration\nDeliverable | Contract Value | SSP | SSP Allocation\nHW/SW | 30 | 30 | 27.90\nServices | 1 | 10 | 3.10\nTotal | 31 | 40 | 31.00\nThe allocation reflects a proportional split based on the list price ratio of 30:10, applied against total contract value of\n31.\n7. Approval Requirements\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 2",
      "metadata": {
        "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-002_v1.0_Order-Intake-Value-SSP-Allocation.pdf",
